//
// Phase C3 operator gate: mha_out_proj.
//
// Fused multi-head attention plus output projection in one ELF: the seq-first
// FlashAttention design's launches followed by the O-projection GEMM's, with
// the attention output staged in a DDR buffer both halves address. No host step
// and no repack between them -- seq-first FlashAttention writes exactly the
// [seq_len, emb_dim] the GEMM reads.
//
// Runs opcheck.py on real NPU2 against an FP32 reference: np.isclose over the
// full output at rtol=1.6e-2, zero permitted mismatches. The reference is
// CHUNKED FP32 attention at every sequence length. iron's oracle computes bf16
// SDPA below seq_len 16384 and switches to FP32 chunked attention at and above
// it, so its own precision changes across the ladder; that branch is dropped
// here on purpose, and restoring it would make a tolerance calibrated at one
// end mean something different at the other.
//
// The reference is FP32 end to end and does not reproduce the bf16 staging of
// the attention output between the two halves. That gap is measured rather than
// defined away, and it is part of what atol is sized against.
//
// Three shapes, checked individually and in order. Causal and non-causal are
// SEPARATE shape keys because masking is a distinct device path and changes the
// arithmetic -- early rows attend to a handful of keys, so the output's dynamic
// range widens by an order of magnitude and the two rows carry different
// tolerances for the same relative error.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipe below. Device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock, which XRTRunner.run_test holds across
// binary load and dispatch (python/air/backend/xrt_runner.py:292) -- the same
// inode lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution and KernelCache take, so this interlocks
// with every other NPU job in the repository while the peano compiles still
// overlap. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here instead would DEADLOCK:
// the gate command that invokes this suite already holds that inode, and BSD
// flock(2) treats a second open() of the same file as a foreign lock, so the
// nested acquire would block against its own parent until the timeout expires.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_mha_out_proj_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_mha_out_proj_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-mha-out-proj PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// The resolved configuration line before each verdict, not just the verdict:
// the design's knobs and the projection's registry-resolved method are what a
// silently mis-shaped run would get wrong, and a test that only read PASS would
// not see it. The causal flag is checked per shape for the same reason -- a
// build that dropped the mask would still emit a correctly-shaped output.
// CHECK: causal=False
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] mha_out_proj [512x512x8h]: PASS
// CHECK: causal=True
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] mha_out_proj [512x512x8h_causal]: PASS
// CHECK: causal=True
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] mha_out_proj [2048x1024x16h_causal]: PASS
